  "history": "EQT Ventures was launched in Stockholm in 2016 by Hjalmar Winbladh, Kees Koolen and Lars Jörnow as the venture capital arm of the Swedish investment group EQT. Its first bets included Wolt, Small Giant Games and Varjo, and it later backed Handshake, Netlify, Einride, Nothing and Parloa. Its third fund, EQT Ventures III, closed in 2022 at EUR 1.1 billion, and the firm has backed more than 140 founding teams.",
